1. The date and manner in which notice of the claim was received, and the identity of the person who provided notice;
2. A copy of the policy, including all endorsements in effect on the date of loss;
3. All correspondence sent to or received from the claimant, including any requests for additional information and responses thereto;
4. A log of all telephone calls or other verbal communications with the claimant, noting the date, time, and substance of the communication;
5. The name and title of every individual who performed work on the claim, and a description of the work performed;
6. All estimates, appraisals, and other valuation documents considered in the evaluation of the claim;
7. Any reports or opinions obtained from independent adjusters, engineers, or other experts;
8. A written explanation of the basis for any coverage determination, including the specific policy provisions relied upon;
9. If the claim is denied, a copy of the denial letter and proof of mailing or other delivery; and
10. Any other document or record that materially bears on the evaluation or resolution of the claim.

**B. Documentation of the Investigation Timeline**

The claim file must clearly document the start and end dates of the investigation, as well as any period during which the investigation was extended under Section III.B. For each extension, the file must include a written explanation of the circumstances beyond the control of the insurer or TPA that necessitated the additional time, and the date on which those circumstances were first identified.

If the insurer or TPA requests additional information from the claimant, the file must document the date of the request, the specific information requested, and the date on which the requested information was received. In the event that the requested information is not received, the file must document the follow-up attempts made and the date on which the insurer or TPA determined that the information was not reasonably necessary to make a coverage determination.

**C. Required Documentation for Coverage Determinations**

Where a claim is denied in whole or in part, the claim file must contain a written coverage analysis that includes:

